- **`turn_signals.c`**: Appended `elapsedMs = 0;` inside the activation block of `SignalLeft()`, `SignalRight()`, and `SignalOff()`. By syncing the millisecond tracker precisely back to `0` at the very instant a UART signal command originates, the internal buzzer logic naturally progresses through its initial `0-100` millisecond pause and perfectly meets the exact `elapsedMs == pauseTimeMs` equality condition check. This robustly clears up the runtime behavioral mismatch causing asynchronous button presses to "skip" initialization.

